  "title": "DVB-S2-TABLE: Fix FCT2 frame_type_section_fix_acc_method bitmask",
  "description": "## Fix incorrect bitmask for FCT2 `frame_type_section_fix_acc_method` field in DVB-RCS2 dissector\n\n### Summary\n\nThe bitmask for the `section_fixed_access_method` field in the FCT2 dissector is incorrect. The current mask `0x0C` selects only 2 bits (bits 3:2), whereas the standard defines the field as a 4-bit value occupying the lower nibble of the byte.\n\n### Standard reference\n\n**ETSI EN 301 545-2 V1.4.1** \"Digital Video Broadcasting (DVB); Second Generation DVB Interactive Satellite System (DVB-RCS2)\" Part 2: Lower Layers for Satellite standard, page 58, FCT2 `fixed_access_method` descriptor:\n\n```\nfixed_access_method: This 4 bit field indicates the access method to be used for the timeslots in frame section\nwhen default_tx_type > 0.\n```\n\nThe field occupies the full lower nibble, i.e. bitmask must be `0x0F`.\n\n### Bug\n\nIn `epan/dissectors/packet-dvb-s2-table.c`, line 576:\n\n```c\n// WRONG — selects only bits 3:2 (2-bit field)\n\n#define DVB_S2_TABLE_FRAME_TYPE_SECTION_FAM_MASK  0xC\n```\n\n`0x0C` = `0000 1100` — this captures only bits 3 and 2, misinterpreting any value where bits 1 or 0 are set.\n\n### Fix\n\n```c\n// CORRECT — selects bits 3:0 (4-bit field per ETSI EN 301 545-2 Table p.57)\n\n#define DVB_S2_TABLE_FRAME_TYPE_SECTION_FAM_MASK  0xF\n```\n\n### Impact\n\n- Wireshark currently displays `.... 00.. = Section fixed access method: 0x0` for packets where bits 1:0 of the field are non-zero, silently dropping part of the value.\n- Any implementation that uses `fixed_access_method` values `0x1`, `0x2`, `0x3` (where only bits 1:0 are set) will be decoded as `0x0`, causing incorrect protocol interpretation.\n- The reserved upper nibble is unaffected.\n\n### Testing\n\nVerify with a FCT2 capture where `fixed_access_method != 0`. Alternatively, craft a synthetic frame with byte value `0x01` at the relevant offset - current code decodes as `0x0`, fixed code decodes as `0x1`.\n\n### References\n\n- ETSI EN 301 545-2 V1.4.1, p. 58: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/301500_301599/30154502/01.04.01_60/en_30154502v010401p.pdf\n- Affected line: `epan/dissectors/packet-dvb-s2-table.c:576`, definition of `DVB_S2_TABLE_FRAME_TYPE_SECTION_FAM_MASK`",
